      "text": "To solve the problem, let's denote the four positive integers as \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\). According to the problem, when these integers are divided by 11, the remainders are 2, 4, 6, and 8, respectively. This can be expressed as:\n\n\\[a \\equiv 2 \\pmod{11}\\]\n\\[b \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11}\\]\n\\[c \\equiv 6 \\pmod{11}\\]\n\\[d \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11}\\]\n\nWe need to find the remainder when the sum of these four integers is divided by 11. First, let's find the sum of the remainders:\n\n\\[2 + 4 + 6 + 8 = 20\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 20 is divided by 11. We perform the division:\n\n\\[20 \\div 11 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 9\\]\n\nSo, the remainder when 20 is divided by 11 is 9. Therefore, the remainder when the sum of the four integers is divided by 11 is also 9.\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{9}\\]",
