      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let's denote the four positive integers as \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\). According to the problem, when each of these integers is divided by 11, they give remainders of 2, 4, 6, and 8 respectively. This can be expressed mathematically as:\n\\[ a \\equiv 2 \\pmod{11} \\]\n\\[ b \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11} \\]\n\\[ c \\equiv 6 \\pmod{11} \\]\n\\[ d \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11} \\]\n\nWe are asked to find the remainder when the sum of these four integers, \\(a + b + c + d\\), is divided by 11. Using the properties of congruences, we can add the congruences together:\n\\[ a + b + c + d \\equiv 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 \\pmod{11} \\]\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the remainders:\n\\[ 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 = 20 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when 20 is divided by 11. We do this by performing the division:\n\\[ 20 \\div 11 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 9 \\]\nThis can be written as:\n\\[ 20 = 11 \\cdot 1 + 9 \\]\n\nThus, the remainder when 20 is divided by 11 is 9. Therefore, the remainder when the sum of the four integers \\(a + b + c + d\\) is divided by 11 is:\n\\[ \\boxed{9} \\]",
