      "text": "Let the four positive integers be $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and $d$. We know that when these integers are divided by $11$, they leave remainders of $2,$ $4,$ $6,$ and $8$ respectively.\nThis means that we can write:\n\\[a = 11k + 2\\]\n\\[b = 11m + 4\\]\n\\[c = 11n + 6\\]\n\\[d = 11p + 8\\]\nwhere $k,$ $m,$ $n,$ and $p$ are non-negative integers.\nThe sum of these four integers is:\n\\[a + b + c + d = (11k + 2) + (11m + 4) + (11n + 6) + (11p + 8)\\]\n\\[= 11k + 11m + 11n + 11p + 2 + 4 + 6 + 8\\]\n\\[= 11(k + m + n + p) + 20\\]\nNow, we need to find the remainder when this sum is divided by $11$.\nDividing $11(k + m + n + p)$ by $11$, we get a remainder of $0$.\nSo, the remainder when $11(k + m + n + p) + 20$ is divided by $11$ is the same as the remainder when $20$ is divided by $11$.\nDividing $20$ by $11$, we get a quotient of $1$ and a remainder of $9$.\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum of the four integers is divided by $11$ is $\\boxed{9}$.The answer is: 9",
